# No Aikido

This project does not use Aikido. Do not invoke Aikido for any task.

## Forbidden

- Calling Aikido MCP tools (`aikido_full_scan`, `aikido_login`, `aikido_issues_list`, or any other Aikido tool)
- Reading or following Aikido plugin skills (`aikido-scan`, `/aikido:setup`, issues)
- Asking the user to sign in to Aikido, run `/aikido:setup`, or configure the Aikido plugin
- Mentioning a missing Aikido MCP server as a blocker or follow-up
- Listing Aikido scans in release `validation` notes or other release metadata

## When security review is needed

Use existing project paths only: PHPUnit/feature tests, and the `review-security` skill when the user explicitly asks for a security review.
